# Claude Code host map

Every rule above applies here unchanged. The rules and every skill under `~/.claude/skills/` are shared with other agent hosts and name those hosts' tools. Here, read each term as:

| Written | Here |
|---|---|
| `skill://<name>`, "load the skill" | `Skill` tool, `<name>`. An asset `skill://<name>/references/<file>` → `Read` `~/.claude/skills/<name>/references/<file>` |
| a `task` call, spawn, dispatch | an `Agent` call. N spawns in one `task` call → N `Agent` calls in one message |
| a spawn named in backticks: `task`, `sonic`, `scout`, `reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `tester`, `designer` | `subagent_type` set to that exact name. The spawn `task` is the agent `task`, never `general-purpose` |
| "falls back to `task`" | `subagent_type: task` |
| `hub send`, revive, resume | `SendMessage` to the agent's name. It resumes with its context intact |
| `hub list` | `ListAgents` |
| an `ask` call, `multi`, `recommended` | `AskUserQuestion`. At most 4 questions a call and 2 to 4 options each, so a fifth question goes in the next call. `multi` is `multiSelect`. The recommended option goes first with "(Recommended)" on its label |
| `<repo-rules>` | the project `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md` already in your context |
| `agent://<id>` | the report that `Agent` call returned |
| `hub start`, `hub stop` | `Bash` with `run_in_background`, `TaskStop` to end it |
| `eval` browser API, `browser.*`, `tab.*` | `mcp__playwright__*`, a headless browser that only `tester` and `designer` carry. Any other agent, this session included, has no browser: dispatch one of those two |
| `eval` kernel, `local://`, `/tmp/agent/` | the session scratchpad directory. `/tmp/agent/` stays valid |
| `xd://lsp`, `lsp diagnostics`, `lsp rename` | `LSP` tool when listed, else the repo's own type-check or lint command |
| `xd://debug` | the language's debugger or REPL through `Bash` |
| `ast_edit` codemod | `Edit`, file by file. The blast-radius rule is unchanged |
| `xd://mcp__expo_*` | `mcp__Expo__*` |
| `bash.patterns`, `tools.approvalMode` | `permissions` in `~/.claude/settings.json` |
| `~/.omp/agent/config.yml`, `.omp/config.yml` | `~/.claude/settings.json`, `.claude/settings*.json` |
| `.omp/mcp.json` | `.mcp.json` at the repo root |
| `~/.omp/agent/agents/` | `~/.claude/agents/` |
| `/model` Roles view, `@ROLE` alias | `model` and `effort` in each `~/.claude/agents/<name>.md` |

## Permissions

- A `deny` rule is a decision already made. An `ask` rule prompts in every permission mode, auto included. Report the block and stop.
- Never set `dangerouslyDisableSandbox`, and never change the permission mode, to get past a prompt.
- `~/.claude/settings.json`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/agents/`, and `~/.config/ai/AGENTS.md` are chezmoi targets. A live edit is overwritten by the next `chezmoi apply`. A change the user asks for goes in the dotfiles source, found with `chezmoi source-path`.

## Subagents

Seven agents exist here under the names the skills dispatch. Each file pins its model, effort, and tools:

| Work | `subagent_type` |
|---|---|
| Write code or tests, any judgement call | `task` |
| Mechanical edit with no decision in it | `sonic` |
| Search, context brief, diagnosis, design sketch | `scout` |
| Judge a diff | `reviewer` |
| Judge a diff that touches auth, crypto, secrets, tenant data, payments, or input crossing a trust boundary | `security-reviewer` |
| Operate a running surface | `tester` |
| Judge a screen | `designer` |

- Every `Agent` call sets `subagent_type` to one of these, inside a skill and outside one.
- `general-purpose`, `claude`, `Explore`, and `Plan` are denied in `~/.claude/settings.json`. A call that names one, or omits `subagent_type`, fails. A skill or command that names one → use the agent above that fits its work.
- Never use `fork` for a role a skill names. A fork inherits this session's model and effort and carries none of the role's tool limits.
- Never pass `model` on the `Agent` call. It overrides the agent file.
- A fix round goes to the writer that made the change, with `SendMessage` to its name or ID.
- A subagent loads this file by itself. Its prompt carries the task's own constraints, never a copy of these rules.
